      <h1 id="understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Understanding identity provider configuration<a href="#understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>As an administrator, you can configure OAuth to specify an identity provider after you install your cluster. Developers and administrators obtain OAuth access tokens to authenticate themselves to the API.</p>
      <p>The OpenShift Container Platform master includes a built-in OAuth server.</p>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-overview_understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Identity providers in OpenShift Container Platform<a href="#identity-provider-overview_understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure identity providers by creating a custom resource (CR) that describes the provider and adding it to the cluster. Identity providers enable user authentication in OpenShift Container Platform beyond the default <code>kubeadmin</code> user.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>OpenShift Container Platform usernames containing <code>/</code>, <code>:</code>, and <code>%</code> are not supported.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <h2 id="supported-identity-providers_understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Supported identity providers<a href="#supported-identity-providers_understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure the following types of identity providers:</p>
      <Fragment set:html={"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n  <th>Identity provider</th>\n  <th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider#configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider\">htpasswd</a></td>\n  <td>Configure the <code>htpasswd</code> identity provider to validate user names and passwordsagainst a flat file generated using<a href=\"http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/programs/htpasswd.html\"><code>htpasswd</code></a>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-keystone-identity-provider#configuring-keystone-identity-provider\">Keystone</a></td>\n  <td>Configure the <code>keystone</code> identity provider to integrateyour OpenShift Container Platform cluster with Keystone to enable shared authentication withan OpenStack Keystone v3 server configured to store users in an internaldatabase.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-ldap-identity-provider#configuring-ldap-identity-provider\">LDAP</a></td>\n  <td>Configure the <code>ldap</code> identity provider to validate user names and passwordsagainst an LDAPv3 server, using simple bind authentication.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-basic-authentication-identity-provider#configuring-basic-authentication-identity-provider\">Basic authentication</a></td>\n  <td>Configure a <code>basic-authentication</code> identity provider for users to log in toOpenShift Container Platform with credentials validated against a remote identity provider.Basic authentication is a generic backend integration mechanism.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-request-header-identity-provider#configuring-request-header-identity-provider\">Request header</a></td>\n  <td>Configure a <code>request-header</code> identity provider to identify users from requestheader values, such as <code>X-Remote-User</code>. It is typically used in combination withan authenticating proxy, which sets the request header value.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-github-identity-provider#configuring-github-identity-provider\">GitHub or GitHub Enterprise</a></td>\n  <td>Configure a <code>github</code> identity provider to validate user names and passwordsagainst GitHub or GitHub Enterprise's OAuth authentication server.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-gitlab-identity-provider#configuring-gitlab-identity-provider\">GitLab</a></td>\n  <td>Configure a <code>gitlab</code> identity provider to use<a href=\"https://gitlab.com/\">GitLab.com</a> or any other GitLab instance as an identityprovider.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-google-identity-provider#configuring-google-identity-provider\">Google</a></td>\n  <td>Configure a <code>google</code> identity provider using<a href=\"https://developers.google.com/identity/protocols/OpenIDConnect\">Google's OpenID Connect integration</a>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/identity_providers/configuring-oidc-identity-provider#configuring-oidc-identity-provider\">OpenID Connect</a></td>\n  <td>Configure an <code>oidc</code> identity provider to integrate with an OpenID Connectidentity provider using an<a href=\"http://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#CodeFlowAuth\">Authorization Code Flow</a>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"} />
      <p>Once an identity provider has been defined, you can <a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/using-rbac#authorization-overview_using-rbac">use RBAC to define and apply permissions</a>.</p>
      <h2 id="removing-kubeadmin_understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Removing the kubeadmin user<a href="#removing-kubeadmin_understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">After you define an identity provider and create a new <code>cluster-admin</code> user, you can remove the <code>kubeadmin</code> to improve cluster security.</p>
      <Alert variant="warning" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Warning</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you follow this procedure before another user is a <code>cluster-admin</code>, then OpenShift Container Platform must be reinstalled. It is not possible to undo this command.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You must have configured at least one identity provider.</li>
      <li>You must have added the <code>cluster-admin</code> role to a user.</li>
      <li>You must be logged in as an administrator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Remove the <code>kubeadmin</code> secrets:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete secrets kubeadmin -n kube-system"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-parameters_understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Identity provider parameters<a href="#identity-provider-parameters_understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The following parameters are common to all identity providers:</p>
      <Fragment set:html={"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n  <th>Parameter</th>\n  <th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n  <td><code>name</code></td>\n  <td>The provider name is prefixed to provider user names to form an identity name.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><code>mappingMethod</code></td>\n  <td>Defines how new identities are mapped to users when they log in. Enter one of the following values:</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"} />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>When adding or changing identity providers, you can map identities from the new provider to existing users by setting the <code>mappingMethod</code> parameter to <code>add</code>.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-default-CR_understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Sample identity provider CR<a href="#identity-provider-default-CR_understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can use a custom resource (CR) to see the parameters and default values that you use to configure an identity provider.</p>
      <p>The following example uses the htpasswd identity provider.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: config.openshift.io/v1\nkind: OAuth\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\nspec:\n  identityProviders:\n  - name: my_identity_provider\n    mappingMethod: claim\n    type: HTPasswd\n    htpasswd:\n      fileData:\n        name: htpass-secret"} lang="yaml" title="Sample identity provider CR" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.identityProviders.name</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the provider name, which is prefixed to provider user names to form an identity name.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.identityProviders.mappingMethod</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies how mappings are established between this provider’s identities and <code>User</code> objects.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.identityProviders.htpasswd.fileData.name</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies an existing secret containing a file generated using <a href="http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/programs/htpasswd.html"><code>htpasswd</code></a>.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-provisioning-user-lookup-mapping_understanding-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Manually provisioning a user when using the lookup mapping method<a href="#identity-provider-provisioning-user-lookup-mapping_understanding-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can manually provision users when the <code>lookup</code> mapping method is enabled. The <code>lookup</code> method disables automatic identity-to-user mapping during login, requiring manual provisioning of each user after configuring the identity provider.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create an OpenShift Container Platform user:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create user <username>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create an OpenShift Container Platform identity:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create identity <identity_provider>:<identity_provider_user_id>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Where <code>&lt;identity_provider_user_id&gt;</code> is a name that uniquely represents the user in the identity provider.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a user identity mapping for the created user and identity:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create useridentitymapping <identity_provider>:<identity_provider_user_id> <username>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Additional resources</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li><a href="https://access.redhat.com/solutions/6006921">How to create user, identity and map user and identity in LDAP authentication for <code>mappingMethod</code> as <code>lookup</code> inside the OAuth manifest</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://access.redhat.com/solutions/7072510">How to create user, identity and map user and identity in OIDC authentication for <code>mappingMethod</code> as <code>lookup</code></a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
